Point CREDENTIALS_DIR at a real on-device path instead of the build host

KNOWN UPSTREAM ISSUE (documented in iv-cloud-gateway_git.bb): auth credential
loading/saving in src/services/auth_services.cc reads/writes
${CREDENTIALS_DIR}/vehicle_credentials.json, but CREDENTIALS_DIR was compiled
in as ${CMAKE_SOURCE_DIR}/credentials -- an absolute build-host source path
that does not exist on the target device at all, and can't be made to exist
there since it's a different filesystem layout entirely. In practice this
means load_vehicle_credentials()/save_vehicle_credentials() can never
succeed on-device: confirmed via journalctl on the real vehicle --
AuthService logs "login successful" (admin login works fine), then
create_vehicle() gets a 409 "vehicle already exists" from the backend
(meaning this VIN registered successfully at some point, likely from a
build where CREDENTIALS_DIR happened to resolve to something real), but
load_vehicle_credentials() then fails with "no credentials file found" and
vechile_login() never completes ("vehicle apiKey/apiSecret not available for
login") -- the gateway runs and relays MQTT/gRPC traffic fine, but is
permanently stuck unauthenticated as a vehicle.

Point CREDENTIALS_DIR at /etc/vehicle-gateway/credentials instead -- a real,
persistent, on-device directory (see iv-cloud-gateway_git.bb's do_install/
pkg_postinst for its creation and iv-gateway:iv-gateway ownership, same
pattern as the existing /etc/vehicle-gateway/.env).

Note: this fixes credential persistence going forward. It does NOT retroactively
recover this VIN's already-issued apiKey/apiSecret from whatever build first
registered it -- the backend still has this VIN registered (409), and those
original credentials were never captured anywhere retrievable. Unblocking
this specific vehicle needs either the original apiKey/apiSecret (if recorded
elsewhere) or the backend team resetting/deleting this VIN's registration so
create_vehicle() gets a fresh 201 instead of 409.

Upstream-Status: Pending [not yet merged on github.com/Yaquod/iv-cloud-gateway]

